Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-core native-build specific]

cmake.bbclass unconditionally prepends cmake-native to DEPENDS for any
recipe that inherits it (cmake-native_%.bbappend:11). Bundled curl
(cmcurl) hardcodes USE_NGHTTP2 and USE_LIBIDN2 ON regardless of any -D
override. Both would require a native DEPENDS that closes back onto
cmake-native itself:

  - nghttp2 inherits cmake directly.
  - libidn2 inherits gtk-doc, which needs python3-native, which needs
    expat-native, which inherits cmake - same cycle, one hop further out.

Disable both in the bundled curl instead; cmake-native has no need for
HTTP/2 multiplexing or internationalized domain names.

Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>

diff --git a/Utilities/cmcurl/CMakeLists.txt b/Utilities/cmcurl/CMakeLists.txt
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/Utilities/cmcurl/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Utilities/cmcurl/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -101,6 +101,6 @@ set(USE_HTTPSRR OFF)
-set(USE_LIBIDN2 ON)
+set(USE_LIBIDN2 OFF)
 set(USE_LIBRTMP OFF)
-set(USE_NGHTTP2 ON)
+set(USE_NGHTTP2 OFF)
 set(USE_NGTCP2 OFF)
 set(USE_OPENSSL_QUIC OFF)
 set(USE_QUICHE OFF)
